{"id":"def:training-coverage-defect","name":"Population training-coverage distance","construction":"For every \(k\in\mathcal K\), define the bounded training critic body
\[
 \mathcal F_k^{\mathrm{tr}}
 =\left\{\sum_{j\in J_k}u_jg_{kj}:\sum_{j\in J_k}|u_j|\le B\right\}
\]
and
\[
 \varepsilon_{\mathrm{tr},k}^2
 =\sup_{h\in\mathcal H_k}
 \left\{
 \|q_h-q_{h^\dagger}\|_{L_2(P_Z)}^2
 -\sup_{f\in\mathcal F_k^{\mathrm{tr}}}
 \left(2E_P[(q_h-q_{h^\dagger})(Z)f(Z)]-E_P[f(Z)^2]\right)
 \right\}.
\]
Equivalently, as proved in \(\texttt{lem:training-coverage-distance-identity}\),
\[
 \varepsilon_{\mathrm{tr},k}^2
 =\sup_{h\in\mathcal H_k}
 \operatorname{dist}_{L_2(P_Z)}^2
 \bigl(q_h-q_{h^\dagger},\mathcal F_k^{\mathrm{tr}}\bigr).
\]
The inner dual problem is a finite-dimensional concave quadratic optimization over an \(\ell_1\)-ball, and the outer problem is over the compact coefficient set defining \(\mathcal H_k\). The relevant geometry is the compact bounded critic body itself, not merely its linear span.","inputs":["k","\mathcal K","g_{kj}","J_k","B","q_h","h^\dagger","\mathcal H_k","P","P_Z"]}

